From 08d188f4bb2234ab05586b272ef1faa36edd907d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: LuneOS <claude.ai@herrie.org>
Date: Mon, 10 Aug 2026 13:09:11 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Make webos_machine_dep() optional

cmake-modules-webos only grew this macro after the 1.6.5 release that LuneOS
carries, so configuring fails outright with "Unknown CMake command". Bumping
cmake-modules-webos distro-wide for one macro is a much larger blast radius
than this needs.

Nothing in audiod uses what the macro provides: its only effect is to add a
-DWEBOS_TARGET_MACHINE_<MACHINE> compiler define, and no file under src/ or
include/ references it. The WEBOS_TARGET_MACHINE variable that the install
rules branch on to pick audiod_internal_device_loading_<machine>.json comes
from webos_cmake.bbclass, not from this macro, so machine selection is
unaffected.

Upstream-Status: Pending
---
 CMakeLists.txt | 10 +++++++++-
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/CMakeLists.txt b/CMakeLists.txt
index ba8df92..1b13179 100644
--- a/CMakeLists.txt
+++ b/CMakeLists.txt
@@ -26,7 +26,15 @@ webos_component(1 0 0)
 webos_add_compiler_flags(ALL "-DAUDIOD_IPC_SERVER -DBOOST_DISABLE_THREADS -D_GNU_SOURCE")
 webos_add_compiler_flags(ALL "-Wall")
 
-webos_machine_dep()
+# cmake-modules-webos only grew webos_machine_dep() after the 1.6.5 that LuneOS
+# carries, and bumping it would touch every webOS component in the distro for
+# the sake of one macro. Nothing here needs what it provides: its only effect is
+# a -DWEBOS_TARGET_MACHINE_<MACHINE> compiler define, which no source file under
+# src/ or include/ reads. The WEBOS_TARGET_MACHINE *variable* the install rules
+# below branch on is supplied independently, by webos_cmake.bbclass.
+if(COMMAND webos_machine_dep)
+    webos_machine_dep()
+endif()
 
 include(FindPkgConfig)
 
